user_prompt:
Map the following data source schema to the ontology.

DATA SOURCE: marinetraffic_vessels (type: stream)

SCHEMA:
  mmsi: text — Maritime Mobile Service Identity, the 9-digit identifier broadcast by the vessel's AIS transponder. Assigned by the flag state, so it changes if the vessel is re-flagged. E.g., 538003913
  imo: text — International Maritime Organization number, a permanent 7-digit identifier that stays with the hull for its whole life, unlike the MMSI. Empty when not known. E.g., 9470959
  ship_id: text — MarineTraffic's own internal vessel identifier. Stable, but specific to this provider. E.g., 713139
  lat: double precision — Latitude of the reported position in WGS84 decimal degrees, between -90 and 90. E.g., 37.388430
  lon: double precision — Longitude of the reported position in WGS84 decimal degrees, between -180 and 180. E.g., 23.871230
  speed: double precision — Speed over ground in tenths of a knot, as broadcast by AIS. Divide by ten to obtain knots: a value of 6 means 0.6 knots.
  heading: integer — True heading of the vessel's bow in degrees from true north, 0 to 359. The value 511 means the heading was not available. Differs from course, which is the direction actually travelled.
  course: integer — Course over ground in degrees from true north, 0 to 359. The direction the vessel is actually moving, which differs from its heading when it is set by wind or current. E.g., 41
  status: text — AIS navigational status code: 0 = under way using engine, 1 = at anchor, 2 = not under command, 3 = restricted manoeuvrability, 4 = constrained by draught, 5 = moored, 6 = aground.
  timestamp: timestamp with time zone — UTC timestamp of the AIS position report. E.g., 2020-10-15T12:21:44.000Z
  dsrc: text — Source of the position report: TER for a terrestrial AIS receiver, SAT for satellite AIS.
  utc_seconds: integer — Seconds field of the UTC time at which the position was recorded, as carried in the AIS position report. E.g., 45
  market: text — MarineTraffic's commercial market segment for the vessel. E.g., TANKERS, CONTAINERS, SUPPORTING VESSELS
  shipname: text — Vessel name as broadcast in AIS Message 5. E.g., SUNNY STAR
  shiptype: text — AIS-coded ship type, a numeric code from 0 to 99 defined by ITU-R M.1371. E.g., 89
  callsign: text — Radio call sign allocated to the vessel by the ITU through its flag state. E.g., V7TZ6
  flag: text — Flag state of the vessel as an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code. E.g., MH for the Marshall Islands
  length: integer — Length overall of the vessel in metres. E.g., 184
  width: double precision — Beam, the maximum width of the vessel, in metres. E.g., 27.43
  grt: integer — Gross registered tonnage, a measure of the vessel's total enclosed volume rather than its weight. E.g., 23313
  dwt: integer — Deadweight tonnage in metric tons: the total weight of cargo, fuel, stores and crew the vessel can carry. E.g., 37857
  draught: integer — Reported draught in tenths of a metre, the depth of the hull below the waterline. Divide by ten for metres: a value of 95 means 9.5 metres.
  year_built: integer — Year in which the vessel was built. E.g., 2010
  ship_country: text — Full name of the flag state, as opposed to the two-letter code in the flag column. E.g., Marshall Is
  ship_class: text — MarineTraffic size or design class for the vessel. E.g., HANDYSIZE, AFRAMAX, FEEDER
  rot: integer — Rate of turn as broadcast by AIS. A positive value indicates a turn to starboard, a negative value a turn to port, and zero no turn. E.g., 0
  type_name: text — Human-readable MarineTraffic ship-type classification. E.g., Oil/Chemical Tanker
  ais_type_summary: text — Coarse ship-type grouping above the detailed type name. E.g., Tanker, Cargo, Passenger
  destination: text — Free-text destination keyed in by the crew and broadcast in AIS Message 5. Often a UN/LOCODE, sometimes a port name, sometimes a placeholder such as FOR ORDERS.
  eta: timestamp with time zone — Estimated time of arrival as broadcast via AIS. Entered manually by the crew and frequently stale. E.g., 2020-10-14T12:00:00.000Z
  l_fore: integer — Distance in metres from the bow to the position of the AIS antenna on the vessel. E.g., 5
  w_left: integer — Distance in metres from the port side to the position of the AIS antenna on the vessel. E.g., 5
  current_port: text — Name of the port the vessel is currently in, resolved by MarineTraffic. Empty while the vessel is under way. E.g., GDANSK
  last_port: text — Name of the last port the vessel departed from. E.g., AGIOI THEODOROI
  last_port_time: timestamp with time zone — UTC timestamp at which the vessel departed the last port. E.g., 2020-10-13T23:39:00.000Z
  current_port_id: text — MarineTraffic internal identifier of the current port. Empty while the vessel is under way.
  current_port_unlocode: text — UN/LOCODE of the current port, the five-character UNECE location code. Empty while the vessel is under way.
  current_port_country: text — ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code of the current port. Empty while the vessel is under way.
  last_port_id: text — MarineTraffic internal identifier of the last port departed. E.g., 29
  last_port_unlocode: text — UN/LOCODE of the last port departed. E.g., GRAGT for Agioi Theodoroi
  last_port_country: text — ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code of the last port departed. E.g., GR
  next_port_id: text — MarineTraffic internal identifier of the predicted next port.
  next_port_unlocode: text — UN/LOCODE of the predicted next port. E.g., EETLL for Tallinn
  next_port_name: text — Name of the next port, predicted by MarineTraffic from voyage forecasting rather than broadcast by the vessel. E.g., TALLINN
  next_port_country: text — ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code of the predicted next port.
  eta_calc: timestamp with time zone — Arrival time predicted by MarineTraffic from voyage forecasting, as distinct from the crew-entered value in the eta column.
  eta_updated: timestamp with time zone — UTC timestamp at which the predicted arrival time was last recomputed.
  distance_to_go: integer — Remaining distance to the destination, in nautical miles. E.g., 0
  distance_travelled: integer — Distance covered so far on the current voyage, in nautical miles. E.g., 74
  avg_speed: double precision — Average speed over the current voyage, in knots. Unlike the raw speed column this is already expressed in knots. E.g., 12.6
  max_speed: double precision — Maximum speed recorded over the current voyage, in knots. E.g., 13.2

